;------------------------------------------------------------------------------
; Converts decimal text into a float, as VAL does: optional spaces and sign, digits, a decimal point, digits, and an
; optional E or e exponent with sign (up to 1000). Overflow is caught quietly through FLOAT_OVERFLOW instead of stopping
; the program.
; A float is d0.l (mantissa high, bit 31 set when normalised), d1.w (mantissa low) and d2.w (exponent, bias $3ff, 1.0 =
; $80000000/$3ff); a negative d2 means a negative number.
; Entry: a0 = text.
; Exit: d0/d1/d2 = float, d2 = -1 if the text is not a number or overflows; a0 = first character after the number;
; FLOAT_OVERFLOW and FLOAT_OVERFLOW_QUIET cleared.
;------------------------------------------------------------------------------
string_to_float:
