;------------------------------------------------------------------------------
; MAT INV a()=b(): inverse of a square matrix by Gauss-Jordan elimination with row pivoting (direct formulas\nfor n = 1
; to 3). Stops early on a break.\nEntry: a0 = a() descriptor (result), a1 = b() descriptor\nExit: d0-d7/a0-a2 changed;
; error 87 if the arrays are not square matrices of the same size\nStack frame as MATDET; $3c = offset of the pivot row,
